  "step5_question": {
    "old_question": "What was the cash conversion cycle of Procter & Gamble (P&G) for fiscal year 2024 (ended June 30, 2024), using average balances (beginning and end of year) and a 365-day year, and how does it compare with fiscal year 2023 on the same basis? Report the cash conversion cycle for both years in days, rounded to one decimal place, and state whether it increased or decreased.",
    "old_ground_truth": "Answer:\n- CCC (days) (FY2023): -42.5\n- CCC (days) (FY2024): -45.8\n- CCC change: decreased\nCalculation:\n- CCC (days) (FY2023): -42.5  [((7,073 + 6,924) / 2) / 42,760 x 365 + ((5,471 + 5,143) / 2) / 82,006 x 365 - ((14,598 + 14,882) / 2) / 42,760 x 365]\n- CCC (days) (FY2024): -45.8  [((7,016 + 7,073) / 2) / 40,848 x 365 + ((6,118 + 5,471) / 2) / 84,039 x 365 - ((15,364 + 14,598) / 2) / 40,848 x 365]\nData used ($ millions unless stated):\n- Accounts payable (FY2022): 14,882\n- Accounts payable (FY2023): 14,598\n- Accounts payable (FY2024): 15,364\n- Accounts receivable (FY2022): 5,143\n- Accounts receivable (FY2023): 5,471\n- Accounts receivable (FY2024): 6,118\n- Cost of products sold (FY2023): 42,760\n- Cost of products sold (FY2024): 40,848\n- Total inventories (FY2022): 6,924\n- Total inventories (FY2023): 7,073\n- Total inventories (FY2024): 7,016\n- Net sales (FY2023): 82,006\n- Net sales (FY2024): 84,039",
    "old_answer": {
      "CCC@FY2023": -42.5,
      "CCC@FY2024": -45.8,
      "CCC_change": "decreased"
